From: Yanqi Zhou <yanqzhou@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] locking: rwsem: export rwsem hook declarations for RT

The RT rwsem code still calls Android rwsem vendor hooks from the common
up_write() and downgrade_write() paths, but the hook declarations are only
included in the !PREEMPT_RT block. Move the rwsem hook include into the
common include section so the RT build sees the declarations too.

Signed-off-by: Yanqi Zhou <yanqzhou@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 kernel/locking/rwsem.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel/locking/rwsem.c b/kernel/locking/rwsem.c
index 60c80c0b4c57..10e47c44a3b2 100644
--- a/kernel/locking/rwsem.c
+++ b/kernel/locking/rwsem.c
@@ -27,11 +27,11 @@
 #include <linux/export.h>
 #include <linux/rwsem.h>
 #include <linux/atomic.h>
 #include <trace/events/lock.h>
+#include <trace/hooks/rwsem.h>
 
 #ifndef CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT
 #include "lock_events.h"
 #include <trace/hooks/dtask.h>
-#include <trace/hooks/rwsem.h>
 
 /*
  * The least significant 2 bits of the owner value has the following
-- 
2.43.0
